    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Sample answers: $2$, $3$ and $8$.\n\nTheir squares and cubes have no digits in common.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}2^2&=2\\times2=4\\\\2^3&=2\\times2\\times2=8\\\\3^2&=3\\times3=9\\\\3^3&=3\\times3\\times3=27\\\\8^2&=8\\times8=64\\\\8^3&=8\\times8\\times8=512\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe pairs $4$ and $8$, $9$ and $27$, and $64$ and $512$ each have no digits in common. Thus $2$, $3$ and $8$ satisfy the condition.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
